WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.213
Here are the seven gates on one page.

2
00:00:02.213 --> 00:00:06.993
The first is done when each product's
FedRAMP status, the actions that run from

3
00:00:06.993 --> 00:00:11.849
a vendor's cloud, and the integration
identities are all recorded and accepted.

4
00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:15.235
The second is done when every
attribute has one writer,

5
00:00:15.235 --> 00:00:20.200
every authority class has one approval
system, and every change class has a lane.

6
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.550
That closes two of the four gaps.

7
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.644
The third is done when HR, Entra
ID and Active Directory are

8
00:00:26.644 --> 00:00:31.250
correlated on the employee I D and
the starting drift is measured.

9
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.318
The fourth is done when findings,
requests and manual work all

10
00:00:35.318 --> 00:00:39.625
arrive in ServiceNow as typed tasks,
each with an owner and a clock.

11
00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:44.842
Part 2 covers the rest: actuating through
a connector or a declared exception,

12
00:00:44.842 --> 00:00:49.220
closing only on a re-read, and
running the tempo with its evidence.
